  "prefLabel": "Ncr 731.18 Permitted Use on Trails",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ncr 731.18 Permitted Use on Trails.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 216-F:2, trails within the statewide trail system shall be available for hiking, nature walks, bird watching, horseback riding, bicycling, ski touring, snowshoeing, and snowmobiling, mushing, and off highway recreational vehicles where permitted. The commissioner shall, as necessary, zone and restrict use of any section of the trails after determining appropriate public uses for such trails.\n\n(b) Other department trails shall be available for the uses listed above in accordance with Ncr 730.\n\n(c) All other trails shall be signed for all other permitted uses not covered in this section, including but not limited to directional, speed limit, seasonal restrictions, and advisory signage.\n\nSource. #14055 EMERGENCY, EXPIRED: 2-15-25\n\nNew. #14291, eff 6-25-25, EXPIRES: 6-25-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ncr700.html"
